{"title":"Career roadmap — Journalist","role":"Journalist","summary":"A Journalist researches, verifies and communicates news and analysis through newspapers, digital media, television, radio, magazines and independent media. With an International Studies/Diplomacy background, a strong niche is international affairs, geopolitics, foreign policy, conflict, diplomacy, global economics and security journalism.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"International Studies / Diplomacy"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build journalism fundamentals, international affairs knowledge, reporting, writing, interviewing and digital-media skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as a reporter/correspondent covering international affairs, politics, business, diplomacy or security"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress into specialised correspondent, senior journalist, bureau/editorial roles or investigative journalism"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead international desks, investigative teams, editorial strategy or independent journalism platforms"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Journalism + international affairs foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"World politics"},{"text":"Indian foreign policy"},{"text":"Political systems"},{"text":"International organisations"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"Global economics"},{"text":"History of international relations"},{"text":"Media and communication fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"News writing"},{"text":"Grammar and editing"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Source evaluation"},{"text":"Current-affairs tracking"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"t